# Targets keep their trailing slash on purpose. /salary-compass/ is a directory
# index in public/, so pointing at /salary-compass makes Pages 308 to the slashed
# form — turning every one of these into two hops for no reason.
#
# Only redirects whose destination exists in THIS project belong here. The rest
# of the retirement map (the ~12 junk sitemap URLs: /home-copy, /test-page12345,
# /club/*-v1-deprecated, /porto-template, ...) lands in Phase 4, once the club
# and partner pages they point at actually exist — a 301 to a 404 is worse than
# the 404 it replaces.
/compensation/compare-salary    /salary-compass/  301
/compensation/compare-salary/   /salary-compass/  301
/compensation/compare-salary/*  /salary-compass/  301
